File Index

/RoomsPage.test.tsx
Purpose: Room list renders once an area opens; editing a field round-trips (checked via the manual/raw-text tab); the Exits & connections panel resolves a local exit target; add allocates the next free vnum in range and selects it; delete is blocked when a reference still points at the room (2026-07-26: now asserts the categorized DeleteBlockersPanel renders, and that its "Go fix it on the Map" button fires onGoToMap with (vnum, file)) and otherwise removes it after window.confirm; an initialTarget opens the right area and selects the right room; the spawn link fires onOpenSpawn with the selected room's vnum. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): switching to a different area (now a 2-area fixture) while a room edit is unsaved prompts to confirm — declined keeps the edit + shows the toolbar's "● unsaved changes" indicator, accepted switches.

/RoomsPage.tsx
Purpose: The Rooms tab — a focused single-room editor (2026-07-26 Areas dashboard redesign: Areas regained full editing too, as an at-a-glance nested view of the whole area; Rooms stays the narrow "edit exactly this room" alternative — both fully functional, neither defers to the other anymore). Same pick-area/list/edit shape as MobsPage/ObjectsPage: useAreaWorkbench() + a room list nav (add via model-ops' addRoom/newRoomTemplate/nextFreeVnum; delete via the shared useDeleteWithBlockers(wb,'room') hook, features/areas/DeleteBlockersPanel.tsx) + the detail pane = RoomEditor (imported cross-directory from features/areas) plus RoomConnections rendered below it as a "how does this room fit into the area" panel. Accepts an initialTarget (ExternalRef) prop for cross-tab hand-off (Map room click, Simulate pane's reverse link) and an onOpenSpawn prop (RoomEditor's "See what spawns here" link). A blocked delete shows DeleteBlockersPanel (categorized, "Go fix it" buttons) instead of a flat wb.err() toast — selectRoom() clears the panel's state (via the hook's clearBlockers) on room switch; onGoToResets/onGoToMap/onGoToMobs/onGoToScripts props wire those buttons (App.tsx: resets/map reuse the existing resetsRoomTarget lift + a mapFocus lift with the room's vnum; mobs/scripts are a plain tab switch, no deep-filter target exists for those two yet) — AreasPage.tsx's RoomDashboardEntry wires the identical prop shape to the same hook, so both tabs' blocked-delete experience is the same code path, not two copies. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): addNewRoom fires a success toast; deletion's success toast is now centralized inside useDeleteWithBlockers itself; AreaSidebar now gets onBeforeOpen={() => wb.confirmDiscard('switch areas')} (Step 5 dirty-guard rollout). Phase G: new `pendingSnippet` prop — a useEffect mirrors addNewRoom's own vnum-allocation flow but seeds the new room from the snippet's saved data (discarding its stored vnum, which is meaningless outside its original area); requires an area already open, otherwise errs and tells the user to pick one first.
